IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpa-dates`
IMPORT `cpa-rules`

-- Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) -- the questions of the PARTY.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who is a party to a civil proceeding in the Supreme, County or Magistrates' Court of Victoria,
-- bringing a claim (an injured person, a worker, a claimant, a beneficiary, an employee) or answering one: "Does the Act
-- apply to my case?", "Which overarching obligations bind me?", "Must I try to settle?", "Must I disclose this
-- document, and by when?", "Who certifies, and who files the proper basis certification?", "What can the court do to me
-- if I breach a case management order or my discovery obligations?", "May I apply for summary judgment, and can it be
-- given against me?", "Must I seek directions before calling an expert, and may I call another?", "Can I be sent to
-- mediation without my consent?". One question (s 10) can also be asked by an individual who is a witness, an expert
-- witness, or a helper of a party (a relative who funds the case). The court, the lawyers and the insurers get no seat:
-- the court's findings, leave and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of cpa-rules.l4. The one duty
-- with a deadline (s 26(2)) is a DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Civil Procedure
-- Act 2010, Version No. 022 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the
-- authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the
-- Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil procedure: the party's questions`

§§ `Whether the Act applies`

@export Does the Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) apply to my court case (ss 3, 4)? It applies to civil proceedings in the Supreme, County and Magistrates' Courts, except proceedings under the Acts section 4(2) lists, in VCAT, or under a prescribed Act.
GIVEN `which court` IS A `Court` @desc Which court the case is in: the Supreme Court, the County Court, the Magistrates' Court, VCAT (the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal), or another court or tribunal
      `is it criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the case is a criminal or quasi-criminal proceeding (a prosecution, committal, bail or sentencing) rather than a civil claim
      `which listed Act` IS AN `Act the proceeding is under` @desc Whether the case is brought under one of the Acts section 4(2) excludes (family violence or personal safety intervention orders, confiscation or proceeds of crime, mental impairment, criminal organisations, children and youth, coroners, the old victims of crime assistance scheme, sentencing, serious offenders, VCAT Part 3A, domestic violence orders, youth justice), or none of them
      `is it under a prescribed Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the case is under an Act that regulations have prescribed as excluded (answer no if unsure; no such regulations are encoded)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the Civil Procedure Act apply to my case` MEANS
    `ss 3, 4 -- the Act applies to the proceeding` `which court` `is it criminal` `which listed Act` `is it under a prescribed Act`

§§ `The overarching obligations`

@export Does this overarching obligation of the Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) bind me (ss 10, 16 to 26)? Parties are bound by all of them; witnesses by none; expert witnesses by all but ss 18, 19, 22 and 26; funders, insurers and other helpers so far as they control or influence the case.
GIVEN `my role` IS A `Role in the proceeding` @desc Your role in the case: a party (you sue or are sued), a witness (not as an expert), an expert witness, or a person who gives a party financial or other help (a relative paying the costs, a litigation funder, an insurer)
      `which obligation` IS AN `Overarching obligation` @desc The overarching obligation you are asking about (ss 16 to 26: the paramount duty, honesty, proper basis, only necessary steps, cooperation, not misleading, trying to settle, narrowing issues, reasonable costs, minimising delay, disclosing critical documents)
      `do I control or influence the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you help a party: whether you exercise any direct or indirect control, or any influence, over how the case or the party is conducted (answer no if you are a party or a witness)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does this overarching obligation bind me` MEANS
    `s 10 -- the overarching obligation applies to me` `my role` `which obligation` `do I control or influence the case`

@export Does the Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) forbid me to make this claim, or this response to a claim (s 18)? Breach can bring costs and other orders (ss 28, 29).
GIVEN `is it frivolous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim or response is frivolous (so lacking in substance that it cannot succeed)
      `is it vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is vexatious (brought to harass or annoy, or for a purpose other than resolving the dispute)
      `is it an abuse of process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is an abuse of the court's process
      `has it a proper basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the facts and law available to you when you make it, the claim or response has a proper basis
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I forbidden to make this claim or response` MEANS
    `s 18 -- I must not make the claim or response` `is it frivolous` `is it vexatious` `is it an abuse of process` `has it a proper basis`

@export Does the Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) forbid me to take this step in my case (s 19)? You may take a step only if you reasonably believe it is necessary to resolve or decide the case.
GIVEN `do I believe it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably believe the step (an application, a subpoena, a further affidavit, a request) is necessary to help resolve or decide the case
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I forbidden to take this step` MEANS
    `s 19 -- I must not take the step` `do I believe it necessary`

@export Must I use reasonable endeavours to settle my dispute by agreement, including by mediation where appropriate (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 22)?
GIVEN `is settling against the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not in the interests of justice to try to resolve the dispute by agreement (a judgment the court may make; answer no if unsure)
      `is only a judge's decision appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dispute is of a kind that only a court's decision is appropriate (for example where a civil penalty is sought)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I try to settle the dispute` MEANS
    `s 22 -- I must try to resolve the dispute by agreement` `is settling against the interests of justice` `is only a judge's decision appropriate`

@export If the whole dispute cannot be settled, must I use reasonable endeavours to agree what I can and narrow the remaining issues (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 23)?
GIVEN `is the whole dispute settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the whole dispute has been resolved by agreement
      `is narrowing against the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is not in the interests of justice to do so (answer no if unsure)
      `is only a judge's decision appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dispute is of a kind that only a court's decision is appropriate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I try to narrow the issues` MEANS
    `s 23 -- I must try to narrow the issues` `is the whole dispute settled` `is narrowing against the interests of justice` `is only a judge's decision appropriate`

§§ `Disclosing critical documents (overarching obligation)`

@export Must I tell the other parties that this document exists (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 26)? The duty covers critical documents you have or had, apart from privileged or legally protected ones, and lasts for the whole case.
GIVEN `have I had it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document is, or has ever been, in your possession, custody or control
      `am I aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are aware of the document
      `is it critical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consider, or ought reasonably to consider, that the document is critical to resolving the dispute
      `is it privileged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document is privileged (for example legal advice to you) and the privilege has not been waived, expressly or by implication
      `is it protected by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act (Victorian or Commonwealth) or other law protects the document from disclosure
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I disclose that this document exists` MEANS
    `s 26 -- I must disclose the existence of the document` `have I had it` `am I aware of it` `is it critical` `is it privileged` `is it protected by law`

@export Was, or is, my disclosure of a critical document in time (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 26(2))? It must be at the earliest reasonable time after you became aware of it, or at the time the court directed.
GIVEN `day I became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware that the document exists
      `did the court direct a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has directed a time for disclosing it
      `day the court directed` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time the court directed (any date if it directed none)
      `earliest reasonable day` IS A DATE @desc The last day that would count as the earliest reasonable time after you became aware (a judgment; used only if the court directed no time)
      `have I disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have told each other party that the document exists
      `day I disclosed it` IS A DATE @desc The day you did so (any date if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Is my disclosure in time` MEANS
    `s 26(2) -- what became of my disclosure` `day I became aware` `did the court direct a time` `day the court directed` `earliest reasonable day` `have I disclosed it` `day I disclosed it` `today`

@export May I use documents or information the other side disclosed to me under the overarching obligation for a purpose outside this case (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 27)? Misuse is contempt of court.
GIVEN `did they agree in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who disclosed them has agreed in writing to the use
      `did the court release me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave releasing you from the obligation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I use disclosed documents outside the case` MEANS
    `s 27 -- I may use the disclosed documents for another purpose` `did they agree in writing` `did the court release me`

@export Can a document exchanged under the overarching disclosure obligation be admitted in evidence in my case (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 27(4))? It must first be discovered.
GIVEN `has it been discovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document has been discovered in the case (listed in an affidavit of documents or produced under discovery)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the exchanged document be admitted` MEANS
    `s 27(4) -- the exchanged document can be admitted` `has it been discovered`

§§ `Sanctions for breaching the overarching obligations`

@export Can the court make orders against me (costs, compensation, penalty interest, steps to fix the breach, a bar on steps) for breaching an overarching obligation (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 29)?
GIVEN `is the court satisfied I breached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied, on the balance of probabilities, that you contravened an overarching obligation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court make orders against me for a breach` MEANS
    `s 29 -- the court may make an order against me` `is the court satisfied I breached`

@export Can I still apply for orders against someone who breached an overarching obligation in my case (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) ss 29 to 31)? Apply before the case is finalised; after that, only with an extension, given only if you did not know of the breach in time.
GIVEN `am I a party or interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a party to the case, or the court considers you have a sufficient interest in it
      `is the case finalised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the case has been finalised, counting the day of the last order made in it (including any costs order) as the day of finalisation, and ignoring any time for an appeal
      `did I not know until after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not aware of the breach until after the case was finalised
      `has the court extended time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has granted you an extension of time
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where I stand on a section 29 application`
`Can I still apply for orders for a breach` MEANS
    `ss 30, 31 -- where I stand on applying under section 29` `am I a party or interested` `is the case finalised` `did I not know until after` `has the court extended time`

§§ `Certification when filing`

@export Is the document I am filing a "substantive document" (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 3)? Your first one carries the overarching obligations certification and, with some later ones, a proper basis certification.
GIVEN `which document` IS A `Kind of document` @desc The kind of document: an originating motion, a writ (with or without a statement of claim), a complaint, a defence, a reply, a counterclaim and responses, third or later party notices, a Transport Accident Act s 93(4)(d) application, an affidavit, summons or application that starts the case or is your first response, a contribution claim, a preliminary discovery claim, or one of the excluded kinds (costs taxation, contempt, rehearing, WorkCover s 299 application, appeals, Corporations Act proceedings, Chapter III originating motions)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my document a substantive document` MEANS
    `s 3 -- the document is a substantive document` `which document`

@export Who must make my overarching obligations certification, that I have read and understood the overarching obligations and the paramount duty (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 41)? It is filed with your first substantive document.
GIVEN `have I a litigation guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a litigation guardian or similar representative acts for you
      `am I without control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of a statute or an insurance contract, you have no meaningful control over how the case is conducted (for example your insurer runs it)
      `have I a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a legal practitioner represents you
      `have I certified elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have personally made the overarching obligations certification in another civil case in the same jurisdiction
      `day I last certified elsewhere` IS A DATE @desc The day you last did so (any date if never)
      `day this case began` IS A DATE @desc The day the current case was commenced
      `months the rules allow` IS A NUMBER @desc The period, in months, the rules of court specify for relying on an earlier certification (0 if they specify none; the Act then allows 2 years)
      `will my lawyer certify it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your lawyer certifies, under the rules of court, that you made the certification in other cases within that period
GIVETH A `Who makes the overarching obligations certification`
`Who makes my overarching obligations certification` MEANS
    `s 41 -- who makes my overarching obligations certification` `have I a litigation guardian` `am I without control` `have I a lawyer` `have I certified elsewhere` `day I last certified elsewhere` `day this case began` `months the rules allow` `will my lawyer certify it`

@export Must a proper basis certification be filed with this document, and by whom (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 42)? It certifies that each allegation, denial and non-admission (or claim and response) has a proper basis on the material available.
GIVEN `which filing` IS A `Document being filed` @desc The document being filed: your first substantive document, a later one that adds or substitutes a party, claim, defence or material allegation or makes a significant amendment, a later one that does none of these, or a document that is not a substantive document
      `do the rules or court require it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules of court or a direction of the court require a proper basis certification with this document
      `is it exempt as administrative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules of court exempt this document from proper basis certification as administrative in nature (for example registering a judgment)
      `have I a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a legal practitioner represents you
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who files the proper basis certification`
`Who files the proper basis certification` MEANS
    `s 42 -- who files the proper basis certification` `which filing` `do the rules or court require it` `is it exempt as administrative` `have I a lawyer`

@export May I file a document now and certify later (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 44)? Only if the filing is urgent (for example a limitation period about to expire); the certification must then follow as soon as practicable.
GIVEN `is it urgent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a matter of urgency, the document must be filed before the certification can be made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I file now and certify later` MEANS
    `s 44 -- I may file now and certify later` `is it urgent`

@export Can the court stop me starting my case, or filing a substantive document, merely because I have not certified (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 45)? Not unless it orders otherwise; it may take the failure into account in costs and other orders (s 46).
GIVEN `has the court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered otherwise
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court stop my filing for want of certification` MEANS
    `s 45 -- the court may stop my filing for want of certification` `has the court ordered otherwise`

§§ `Case management (arises if you are said to have breached a direction or order)`

@export If I breach a case management direction or order, can the court impose this sanction on me (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 51)?
GIVEN `did I breach it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contravened a direction given, or an order made, by the court under Part 4.2 (case management, timetables, pre-trial and trial procedure)
      `my side` IS A `Side` @desc Whether you are a plaintiff (you brought the claim) or a defendant (the claim is against you)
      `which sanction` IS A `Case management sanction` @desc The sanction you are asking about: dismissal, striking out your claim, striking out your defence with judgment, striking out a document, rejecting evidence, costs, or any other order
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court impose this case management sanction on me` MEANS
    `s 51 -- the court may impose the sanction on me` `did I breach it` `my side` `which sanction`

§§ `Discovery`

@export Under a consent order to give the other side all my documents (s 55A), may I hold back privileged documents (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 55A(4))? At your own expense; you must then list them with the grounds of privilege.
GIVEN `is there a section 55A order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, with all parties' consent, has ordered or directed you to provide all documents relating to the issues to another party
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I hold back privileged documents` MEANS
    `s 55A(4) -- I may hold back privileged documents` `is there a section 55A order`

@export Must I give the other party a list of the privileged documents I held back, with the grounds (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 55A(5))?
GIVEN `is there a section 55A order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court, with all parties' consent, has ordered or directed you to provide all documents relating to the issues to another party
      `did I hold any back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you excluded any privileged documents before providing them
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I list the privileged documents` MEANS
    `s 55A(5) -- I must give a list of the privileged documents` `is there a section 55A order` `did I hold any back`

@export Can the court impose this sanction on me for a discovery failure (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 56)?
GIVEN `what the court found` IS A `Discovery finding` @desc What the court has found: no such finding, a failure to comply with discovery obligations, a failure to comply with a discovery order or direction, or conduct intended to delay, frustrate or avoid discovery
      `am I responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person responsible for the failure or conduct
      `which sanction` IS A `Discovery sanction` @desc The sanction you are asking about (contempt proceedings, adjournment costs, costs including indemnity costs, a bar on steps, limits on documents in evidence, facts taken as established, compensation, an adverse inference, compelled evidence, dismissal of part of your claim or defence, or any other order)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court impose this discovery sanction on me` MEANS
    `s 56 -- the court may impose the discovery sanction on me` `what the court found` `am I responsible` `which sanction`

@export May I cross-examine, or seek leave to examine orally, the person who swore the other side's affidavit of documents (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 57)?
GIVEN `have I a reasonable basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a reasonable basis for believing the other party may be misreading its discovery obligations or failing to disclose discoverable documents
      `has the court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered otherwise
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I cross-examine on the affidavit of documents` MEANS
    `s 57 -- I may cross-examine the deponent of the other side's affidavit of documents` `have I a reasonable basis` `has the court ordered otherwise`

§§ `Summary judgment`

@export May I apply for summary judgment (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) ss 60 to 62)? A plaintiff applies on the ground that the defence has no real prospect of success; a defendant on the ground that the claim has none.
GIVEN `my side` IS A `Side for summary judgment` @desc Whether you are a plaintiff (or plaintiff by counterclaim), a defendant (or defendant by counterclaim), or another party such as a third party
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I apply for summary judgment` MEANS
    `ss 61, 62 -- I may apply for summary judgment` `my side`

@export Can the court give summary judgment against me (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) ss 63, 64)?
GIVEN `is the court satisfied I have no real prospect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that your claim, defence or counterclaim (or part of it) has no real prospect of success
      `who moves` IS A `Who moves for summary judgment` @desc Whether the other side applied, or the court is acting of its own motion
      `is the court satisfied it is desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the court acts of its own motion: whether it is satisfied that summarily disposing of the case is desirable
      `has the court sent it to trial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered under s 64 that the case proceed to trial despite no real prospect of success
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court give summary judgment against me` MEANS
    `ss 63, 64 -- the court may give summary judgment against me` `is the court satisfied I have no real prospect` `who moves` `is the court satisfied it is desirable` `has the court sent it to trial`

@export Even if my case has no real prospect of success, can the court let it go to trial (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 64)?
GIVEN `is summary disposal against the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that disposing of the case summarily is not in the interests of justice
      `is only a full hearing appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that the dispute is of a kind where only a full hearing on the merits is appropriate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my case go to trial despite no real prospect` MEANS
    `s 64 -- the court may send my proceeding to trial despite no real prospect` `is summary disposal against the interests of justice` `is only a full hearing appropriate`

§§ `Expert evidence`

@export Must I seek the court's direction before using expert evidence at trial (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 65G)? As soon as practicable after you intend, or become aware you may, to call it.
GIVEN `which court` IS A `Court` @desc Which court the case is in
      `do the Magistrates' Court rules apply it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Magistrates' Court only: whether its rules of court apply the requirement to your kind of case
      `will I call expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to adduce expert evidence at trial, or have become aware that you may
      `do the rules or court say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules of court provide otherwise or the court has ordered otherwise
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I seek directions about expert evidence` MEANS
    `s 65G -- I must seek the court's direction about expert evidence` `which court` `do the Magistrates' Court rules apply it` `will I call expert evidence` `do the rules or court say otherwise`

@export May I call evidence from my own, other expert on an issue already covered by a joint experts report, a single joint expert or a court appointed expert (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) ss 65J(4), 65O)? Only with the court's leave.
GIVEN `is there a joint report on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a joint experts report deals with the issue and you are a party affected by it
      `is there a single joint expert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a single joint expert has been engaged on the issue
      `is there a court expert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court appointed expert has been appointed on the issue
      `has the court given leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given you leave to call the other expert
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I call another expert on the issue` MEANS
    `ss 65J(4), 65O -- I may call another expert on the issue` `is there a joint report on it` `is there a single joint expert` `is there a court expert` `has the court given leave`

@export Am I forbidden to approach a proposed single joint expert for an opinion (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 65L(6)(a))?
GIVEN `do I know they are being considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know the person is under consideration for engagement as a single joint expert
      `are they engaged already` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has already been engaged
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I forbidden to approach the proposed joint expert` MEANS
    `s 65L(6)(a) -- I must not seek the person's opinion` `do I know they are being considered` `are they engaged already`

@export Must I tell the other parties about my earlier communications with a proposed single joint expert (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 65L(6)(b))?
GIVEN `do I know they are being considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know the person is under consideration for engagement as a single joint expert
      `have I spoken to them before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have communicated with the person before on the issues concerned
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I disclose my earlier contact with the proposed joint expert` MEANS
    `s 65L(6)(b) -- I must tell the other parties of my earlier communications` `do I know they are being considered` `have I spoken to them before`

@export Must the parties, me included, seek the court's directions on the instructions to a single joint or court appointed expert (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 65N)? Only if they cannot agree the instructions and the facts and assumptions.
GIVEN `is there such an expert` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a single joint expert has been engaged or a court appointed expert appointed
      `have we agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties have agreed the written instructions and the facts and assumptions of fact for the expert's report
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I seek directions on the expert's instructions` MEANS
    `s 65N(2) -- I must seek directions on the expert's instructions` `is there such an expert` `have we agreed`

@export May I apply for an order that an expert disclose the terms of their retainer, including any fee contingent on the outcome (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 65P(1))?
GIVEN `do the rules say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules of court provide otherwise
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I seek disclosure of an expert's retainer` MEANS
    `s 65P(1) -- I may apply for disclosure of an expert's retainer` `do the rules say otherwise`

@export May I put evidence of an expert's retainer disclosure before the court at trial (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 65P(4))?
GIVEN `has the court given leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I use the retainer disclosure at trial` MEANS
    `s 65P(4) -- I may adduce evidence of the retainer disclosure at trial` `has the court given leave`

§§ `Appropriate dispute resolution`

@export Can the court send my case to mediation or another dispute resolution process without my consent (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 66)? Not to arbitration, a special referee, expert determination or another binding process.
GIVEN `which process` IS AN `Kind of appropriate dispute resolution` @desc The process: mediation, early neutral evaluation, a judicial resolution conference, a settlement conference, conciliation, arbitration, a special referee, expert determination, or another process with or without a binding outcome
      `do the rules say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules of court provide otherwise for this kind of referral (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court send my case to dispute resolution without my consent` MEANS
    `s 66(2) -- the court may send my case to dispute resolution without my consent` `which process` `do the rules say otherwise`

@export Can what was said or done at a judicial resolution conference be given in evidence (Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) s 67)?
GIVEN `did the court order it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court ordered the judicial resolution conference
      `does the court order otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court orders, in the interests of justice and fairness, that the evidence be admitted
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the conference be given in evidence` MEANS
    `s 67 -- what was said at the judicial resolution conference can be given in evidence` `did the court order it` `does the court order otherwise`
